l Bull</source><year>1993</year><volume>185</volume><fpage>302</fpage><lpage>303</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Pierson ES, Smith PJS, Shipley AM et al. Ca2+ fluxes around pollen grains and pollen tubes of lily; normal development and effect of temperature shock, BAPTA-type buffer microinjection and depletion of boric acid from the medium. Biol Bull 1993; 185: 302&#x02013;. </citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brault</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Caiveau</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Pedron</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Detection of membrane-bound cytokinin-binding proteins in <italic>Arabidopsis thaliana</italic> cells</article-title><source>Eur J Biochem</source><year>1999</year><volume>260</volume><fpage>512</fpage><lpage>519</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1432-1327.1999.00190.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Brault M, Caiveau O, Pedron J et al. Detection of membrane-bound cytokinin-binding proteins in Arabidopsis thaliana cells. Eur J Biochem 1999; 260: 512&#x02013;. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10095789</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dubyak</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name><name><surname>El-Moatassim</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Signal transduction via P2-purinergic receptors for extracellular ATP and other nucleotides</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><year>1993</year><volume>265</volume><fpage>C577</fpage><lpage>C606</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Dubyak GR, El-Moatassim C. Signal transduction via P2-purinergic receptors for extracellular ATP and other nucleotides. Am J Physiol 1993; 265: C577&#x02013;06. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8214015</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sauer</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hescheler</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Wartenberg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mechanical strain-induced Ca<sup>2+</sup> waves are propagated via ATP release and purinergic receptor activation</article-title><source>Am J Physiol, Cell Physiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>279</volume><fpage>C295</fpage><lpage>C307</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Sauer H, Hescheler J, Wartenberg M. Mechanical strain-induced Ca2+ waves are propagated via ATP release and purinergic receptor activation. Am J Physiol, Cell Physiol 2000; 279: C295&#x02013;07. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10912995</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bowler</surname><given-names>WB</given-names></name><name><surname>Buckley</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Gartland</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Extracellular nucleotide signaling: A mechanism for integrating local and systemic responses in the activation of bone remodeling</article-title><source>Bone</source><year>2001</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>507</fpage><lpage>512</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S8756-3282(01)00430-6</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bowler WB, Buckley KA, Gartland A et al. Extracellular nucleotide signaling: A mechanism for integrating local and systemic responses in the activation of bone remodeling. Bone 2001; 28: 507&#x02013;2. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11344050</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boyum</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Guidotti</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of ATP binding cassette/multidrug resistance proteins on ATP efflux of <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic></article-title><source>Biochem Biophys Res Commun</source><year>1997</year><volume>230</volume><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/bbrc.1996.5913</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Boyum R, Guidotti G. Effect of ATP binding cassette/multidrug resistance proteins on ATP efflux of Saccharomyces cerevisiae. Biochem Biophys Res Commun 1997; 230: 22&#x02013;. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9020050</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Rajagopal</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Windsor</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A role for ectophosphatase in xenobiotic resistance</article-title><source>Plant Cell</source><year>2000</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>519</fpage><lpage>533</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1105/tpc.12.4.519</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Thomas C, Rajagopal A, Windsor B et al. A role for ectophosphatase in xenobiotic resistance. Plant Cell 2000; 12: 519&#x02013;3. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10760241</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Handa</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Guidotti</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Purification and cloning of a soluble ATP-diphosphohydrolase (apyra